                    "name": "成功",
                    "data": "{\"ok\":true,\"task_name\":\"instrument_brief\",\"session_id\":\"apifox-instrument-brief-ok\",\"result\":{\"instrument_name_or_code\":\"VOO\",\"instrument_type\":\"ETF\",\"overview\":\"VOO is an ETF designed to track the S&P 500 Index. According to the source, it holds a diversified portfolio of large-cap U.S. companies and follows an index-tracking approach rather than active stock selection. Its value may move up or down with the broader U.S. equity market.\",\"key_facts\":[{\"label\":\"Instrument type\",\"value\":\"VOO is an exchange-traded fund (ETF).\"},{\"label\":\"Investment objective\",\"value\":\"It seeks to track the performance of the S&P 500 Index.\"},{\"label\":\"Portfolio description\",\"value\":\"The fund holds a diversified portfolio of large-cap U.S. companies.\"},{\"label\":\"Management style\",\"value\":\"Its objective is index tracking, not active stock selection.\"},{\"label\":\"Market sensitivity\",\"value\":\"Its value can rise or fall with the broader U.S. equity market.\"}],\"learning_points\":[\"Index-tracking funds aim to follow a benchmark rather than beat it.\",\"The S&P 500 is the reference index mentioned in the source material.\",\"ETF value can move with the overall market, not just individual company news.\",\"Diversification can reduce single-company dependence, but it does not remove market risk.\"],\"risk_notes\":[\"The fund's value can decline when the broader U.S. equity market falls.\",\"Because it tracks an index, it is not trying to avoid market downturns through active stock picking.\",\"The source material does not say how diversified the portfolio is beyond describing it as diversified.\",\"The material does not provide fee, holdings, or rebalancing details, so those aspects cannot be evaluated here.\"],\"follow_up_questions\":[\"How does an index-tracking ETF like VOO differ from an actively managed fund?\",\"What does it mean for an ETF to track the S&P 500 Index?\",\"How does exposure to large-cap U.S. companies affect an ETF's behavior?\",\"What information would be needed to evaluate VOO more fully, such as fees or holdings?\"],\"risk_notice\":\"This brief is for educational purposes only and is not investment advice.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The provided material is limited. It does not include fees, exact holdings, expense ratio, distribution details, or current fund data, so those cannot be summarized from the source.\"},\"error\":null}",
